{
  "format": "solstice-test-control-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "edit-brush-strokes-tool",
  "description": "The Edit Brush Strokes Tool on a brush stroke of a vector layer: dragging its middle moves that part of the line, a drag in Change Width changes the picture, a click in Cut makes an undo step and leaves the line in place; a click selects the line and the Apply buttons give it the current color, background color (one undo step; a brush that does not use it looks the same), brush size and brush; Simplify Lines makes one undo step, leaves the line where it is, and has nothing left to take the second time; Add Point with a drag adds a point and moves it, Delete Point removes one with a click, Switch Corner switches one with a click, each one undo step; a drag to the left in Change Density makes the black line gray in the middle (seen over the white background) and leaves it 60 pixels away as it was; a drag to the right in Add Width makes the line 25 pixels wider in the middle (ink 14 pixels above its path, where it was white) and leaves the place 60 pixels along the line white; in Free Transform a click selects the line, a drag inside its frame moves it 50 pixels down and a drag of the frame's bottom side stretches it downwards, one undo step each; in Redraw an arc drawn from one place of the line to another replaces the part between them (ink on the arc, none where the middle was, the ends as they were), one undo step; in Redraw Width a trace along 60 pixels of the line with a brush of 60 pixels makes that part as wide (ink 23 pixels above the path, where it was white) and leaves the line 60 pixels further as it was, one undo step; everything is undone to the drawn line. Create Assistants on the selected line makes one undo step that leaves the picture as it is. Select Inside on the straight line, which encloses nothing, makes no selection and no undo step. The Add Width and Free Transform drags stay within the 228 pixels of canvas that a fresh profile shows after view_reset, which they call first: a drag outside the canvas scrolls the view while the remaining points keep their widget positions.",
